audio AIDL HAL（ModulePrimary）：播放块大小由 ro.vendor.audio.primary.out_latency_ms 决定 —— 让 AudioFlinger 开 FastMixer、游戏拿到 FAST 轨道

应用到 AOSP 树的 hardware/interfaces，由 scripts/crdroid-tree-fixes.py 第 22 条自动应用（幂等）。⚠️ 别往内核树上打。

ModulePrimary::getNominalLatencyMs() 对非 MMAP 流写死 85 ms（注释原文：给模拟器过 CTS 用，真硬件应该低得多），
经 Module::calculateBufferSizeFramesForPcm 取成 4096 帧。AudioFlinger 只在 HAL 块短于 20 ms 时开 FastMixer
（Threads.cpp kMinNormalSinkBufferSizeMs / initFastMixer），于是游戏的 AAudio 低延迟请求一律被拒，
轨道 8196 帧 + 混音 4096 + ALSA 4 × 1440（120 ms）：应用按时间戳算出的输出延迟中位 317 ms（2026-10-09 实测）。

改法：只动输出方向。属性没设时仍是 85 ms（行为不变）；device.mk 设 10 ⇒ 480 帧。
播放由 0069 直接阻塞写 ALSA，块小只是写得更勤；alsa_utils 把块分成 4 个 period（480/4 = 120），
tinyalsa 用 param_set_min 请求、内核 q6apm-dai 按 480 帧步长上调 ⇒ ALSA 4 × 480 = 40 ms，不用另改。
采集保持 85 ms：0052 的 MonoPipe 容量与 0063 的数据驱动交付都是按 4096 调的。
依赖 0069（播放直接写 ALSA）：没有它，小块会落进墙钟定拍 + 非阻塞管道那条路。

--- a/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #define LOG_TAG "AHAL_ModulePrimary"
 #include <Utils.h>
 #include <android-base/logging.h>
+#include <android-base/properties.h>

 #include "core-impl/ModulePrimary.h"
 #include "core-impl/StreamMmapStub.h"
@@ -163,7 +164,20 @@
     // the virtual Android device implementation to pass CTS. Hardware implementations
     // should have significantly lower latency.
     static constexpr int32_t kStandardLatencyMs = 85;
-    return hasMmapFlag(portConfig.flags.value()) ? kLowLatencyMs : kStandardLatencyMs;
+    if (hasMmapFlag(portConfig.flags.value())) return kLowLatencyMs;
+    // gaokun3: the playback block is what AudioFlinger sizes its mixer by. At 85 ms (4096 frames)
+    // there is no FastMixer (it starts only when the HAL buffer is shorter than the 20 ms normal
+    // sink, Threads.cpp kMinNormalSinkBufferSizeMs), FAST requests from games are denied, and a
+    // tap sound waits behind a 2-block client buffer + 85 ms + the ALSA buffer. Playback writes
+    // straight into ALSA and blocks there (StreamPrimary::writesPlaybackDirectly()), so a small
+    // block only means more, shorter writes; the ALSA buffer keeps four periods of it (the
+    // q6apm period step is 480 frames, so a 10 ms block gives 4 x 480 frames = 40 ms).
+    // Capture keeps 85 ms: its MonoPipe sizing and data-driven delivery were tuned for 4096.
+    if (portConfig.flags->getTag() == AudioIoFlags::output) {
+        return ::android::base::GetIntProperty("ro.vendor.audio.primary.out_latency_ms",
+                                               kStandardLatencyMs, 1, kStandardLatencyMs);
+    }
+    return kStandardLatencyMs;
 }

 }  // namespace aidl::android::hardware::audio::core
